 Sciences Inc., a clinical stage biopharmaceutical company, engages in the research, development, and commercialization of therapeutics to treat retinal diseases. Its lead product candidate is tarcocimab tedromer (KSI-301), an anti-vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) antibody biopolymer that has complete Phase 3 clinical study to treat high prevalence retinal vascular diseases; and in Phase 3 clinical study for the treatment of diabetic retinopathy, wet age-related macular degeneration (AMD), retinal vein occlusion, and diabetic macular edema, as well as in Phase 2/3 clinical study to treat wet AMD. The company's preclinical stage product candidate includes KSI-501, an anti- interleukin-6 (IL-6) and VEGF-trap bispecific antibody biopolymer conjugate for high prevalence retinal vascular diseases; and KSI-101 (KSI-501P), a bispecific protein targeting IL-6 and VEGF developed for patients who have retinal fluid and inflammation. The company was formerly known as Oligasis, LLC and changed its name to Kodiak Sciences Inc. in September 2015. Kodiak Sciences Inc. was incorporated in 2009 and is based in Palo Alto, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Victor  Perlroth M.D. | Co-Founder, Chairman, CEO & President | Age 51 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 141 people. Stock-based compensation of $417K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Kodiak Sciences Inc is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $6.2B market cap.","Returns on capital run at -438% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $137M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -26.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (21.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.644625912063816},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 257% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (86% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $176.4M) \u